<section {{ cls }}="mx-auto w-full max-w-5xl flex-1 px-6 py-20">
  <h1 {{ cls }}="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">About</h1>
  <p {{ cls }}="mt-5 max-w-xl text-base leading-7 text-foreground-second">
    Nexy puts routing, rendering and the API in one Python project. Backend developers keep the
    language they know, and the frontend keeps the tools it likes: {{ fw_label }}, Vite and hot reload.
  </p>
  <p {{ cls }}="mt-4 max-w-xl text-base leading-7 text-foreground-second">
    It is open source under the MIT license.
  </p>
  <div {{ cls }}="mt-8 flex gap-3">
    <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" {{ cls }}="btn-primary">Documentation</a>
    <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" {{ cls }}="btn-ghost">GitHub</a>
  </div>
</section>
